# IMPORTANT: git does NOT support trailing inline comments on a pattern line. The
# whole line is treated as the pattern. Keep every comment on its own line.

# Credentials. An API key grants read access to patient data, so it is treated
# like a password and must never be committed under any name.
# Note the hyphen and underscore spellings are BOTH needed: the file Moveshelf
# hands you is mvshlf-api-key.json, which "*api_key*" does not match.
api_key.txt
api_key.dat
*api_key*
*api-key*
*apikey*
*.key
mvshlf-config.json

# The example holiday file is committed; a real one is not.
!holidays.txt.example

# The setup-guide screenshots are pictures of the Moveshelf interface, not
# credentials. They collide with the "*api-key*" glob above, which would have
# silently dropped api-keys.png and left the guide unbuildable from a clone.
!docs/screenshots/*.png

# Real site details (server paths, contact address) for building the guide.
# The tracked docs hold placeholders; this fills them in locally.
docs/site.local.json

# Per-user runtime files written next to the exe. Site-specific, not code.
settings.json
therapists.csv
holidays.txt

# Audit log. Contains no patient identifiers, but it is operational, not source.
logs/

# Internal planning notes and the rollout log. Kept locally only.
PLAN.md
ROLLOUT.md

# Anything captured from the API while developing. Assume it holds PHI.
fixtures/live/
*.live.json
scratch/

# Build output
build/
dist/
*.spec

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
